3194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562777 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562777 1077 "field-1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562777 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562773 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562777 1079 #uuid "187ca06a-34b2-52f2-bb4c-69c7613a1bfe" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562771 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562778 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562778 1077 "field-1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562778 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562771 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562778 1079 #uuid "3bf53a58-c815-5351-a1ce-001a880e2d2f" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562779 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562770 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562779 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562779 1077 "field-1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562779 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562770 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562779 1079 #uuid "56c69cd5-07d2-598b-b43c-0e186d6e3185" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562769 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562780 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562780 1077 "field-1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562780 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562769 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562780 1079 #uuid "69bddd2d-4ab6-5d13-b5cd-247cb058b864" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562774 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562781 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562781 1077 "field-1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562781 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562774 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562781 1079 #uuid "c3549239-369c-5dc5-b97f-5b91a23e416d" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562772 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562782 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562782 1077 "field-2" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562782 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562772 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562782 1079 #uuid "ee0751b7-37b1-5581-b463-69aae210a148" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048652 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048826 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049074 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049399 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050396 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050622 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051017 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1089 #edb/ref 17592186562784 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562783 1090 #uuid "e8d03789-dde0-513c-a07d-47ec47074087" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562793 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562794 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562795 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562796 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562797 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562798 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1084 #edb/ref 17592186562799 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1085 "The sales manager of a company that produces wooden furniture analyses the weekly profit made by creating $x$ wooden tables per week. They found that the weekly profit $p(x),$ in dollars, can be modeled by the quadratic function\n\n$$\np(x)=a{x}^{2}+bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants." 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1086 #uuid "bb1bcb11-dd3e-5ef2-acf5-2bd2feb4ce5d" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562784 1087 #edb/ref 17592186562797 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562777 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1069 "q-167217" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1071 "If the company produces fifteen wooden tables in a week, the weekly profit will be $\\$4\\,050.$ Find an expression for $b$ in terms of $a.$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1072 #uuid "354145f6-5e93-540e-9ff9-3f90c1a259ed" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562785 1074 "In part 1, we found that $p(15)=225a+15b.$ So, we need to solve the equation $225a+15b=4\\,050$ for the parameter $b.$\n\nWe need to isolate the variable $b.$ To do this, we treat $a$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $225a$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}225a+15b & =4\\,050 \\\\ 225a+15b-225a & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ 15b & =4\\,050-225a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15b & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ \\frac{15b}{15} & =\\frac{4\\,050-225a}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{15}b}{\\cancel{15}} & =\\frac{4\\,050}{15}-\\frac{225a}{15} \\\\ b & =270-15a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $b=270-15a.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562776 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1069 "q-167216" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1071 "In terms of $a$ and $b,\\,p(15)=\\,${{field-1}}." 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1072 #uuid "3979b7c5-84a5-5fc8-9e6c-343a28511a49" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562786 1074 "We substitute $x=15$ into the expression for $p(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a{x}^{2}+bx \\\\ p(15) & =a(15)^{2}+b(15) \\\\  & =225a+15b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p(15)=225a+15b.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562779 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1069 "q-167220" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1071 "The manager wants to determine the number of wooden tables the company should produce per week to make a weekly profit of $\\$4\\,800.$ The required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800=0.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be factored as $\\,$$6\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}} $)=0.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1072 #uuid "497dcd2a-064b-5508-ade6-dffd4f30752c" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562787 1074 "We factor $6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800$ using the greatest common factor (GCF).\n\nComputing the GCF, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(6{x}^{2},360x,4\\,800)=6\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800 & = \\\\ 6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800) & = \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-60x+800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${x}^{2}-60x+800.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562778 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1069 "q-167219" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1071 "Determine the weekly profit if the company produces $24$ wooden tables in a week.\n\nThe company will earn$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$dollars." 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1072 #uuid "527dba5f-2797-5f00-97de-509f725bd58d" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562788 1074 "From part 3, we have the function $p(x)=-6{x}^{2}+360x.$\n\nWe substitute $x=24$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(24) & =-6(24)^{2}+360(24) \\\\  & =-3\\,456+8\\,640 \\\\  & =5\\,184\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the company will earn $$5\\,184.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562775 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562782 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1069 "q-167218" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1071 "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $100a+15b=4\\,800.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1072 #uuid "b42bde79-43e7-5e0d-aa7f-ed2b4b36837d" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562789 1074 "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}b=270-15a \\\\ 100a+15b=4\\,800\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=270-15a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100a+15b & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+15(270-15a) & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+4\\,050-225a & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a+4\\,050 & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a & =750 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=270-15a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =270-15(-6) \\\\ b & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=360.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562780 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1069 "q-167221" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1071 "Find the minimum number of wooden tables the company needs to produce per week to make a weekly profit of $\\$4\\,800.$\n\nThe company needs to produce$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ wooden tables per week." 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1072 #uuid "f01f8f3f-d44f-517a-a672-79bef06856d4" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562790 1074 "From part 5, the required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6\\cdot ({x}^{2}-60x+800)=0.\n$$\n\nDividing this equation by $6,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-60x+800=0.\n$$\n\nTo solve this equation, we want to find a factor pair of the constant term $(800)$ that also adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-60).$ The required factors are $(-20)$ and $(-40).$\n\nUsing this factor pair, we write the linear term as $-60x=-20x-40x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-60x+800 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-20x)+(-40x+800) & =0 \\\\ x(x-20)-40(x-20) & =0 \\\\ (x-20)(x-40)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solutions are $x=20$ or $x=40.$ Since we require the minimum solution, we conclude that the company needs to produce $20$ wooden tables per week to make a profit of $$4\\,800.$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562781 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1069 "q-167222" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1071 "The company wants to increase its output by implementing a new production model. The number of wooden tables ${a}_{n}$ produced in the $n$th week since the implementation of the new model is given by the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+4,\\,{a}_{1}=12,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nWhat is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence?\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1072 #uuid "f85c7e50-3cac-5133-ab86-e4e54ecc65fa" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562791 1074 "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=12,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+4 \\\\  & =12+4 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =16-12 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=12$ and $d=4$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =12+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =12+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=4n+8,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562792 1062 #uuid "1befb3fc-18d4-5289-828d-35a76c78d3b1" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562792 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562783 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562793 1062 #uuid "270ae88f-7164-59c9-b5e2-e9c6bfa91401" 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562793 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562791 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562794 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562795 13194139536061 17592186045417 true] [17592186562794 1062 #uuid "482fe2ee-b30e-5f6b-bdcd-e64c9ab1d2eb" 131941395